-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata --ci` (MJ CLI 6.1.5) against a database built from
-- migrations ONLY: MJ core v6.1.5, bizapps-common v5.52.0, bizapps-tasks v1.7.0,
-- bizapps-accounting v0.22.0, bizapps-orders v5.30.0, bizapps-contracts v0.7.3, then this app's
-- migrations at `next`. Push result: 0 created, 4 updated, 211 unchanged, 0 errors (plus the one
-- derived query field below).
--
-- WHY. The close-date / date-only display fix (bc-aidp-next-golive#168) changed the SQL of four
-- queries as metadata only, so no migration carried it and the 6.12 release seed gate refused to
-- publish: hosts would keep the old SQL, which compares against the UTC day instead of the
-- business day.
--
-- UPDATED, each checked against the latest earlier seed of the same ID; every change traces to
-- metadata/queries:
--   * SQL and TechnicalDescription of `Sales: Dashboard Summary`, `Sales: Deal Cycle Time`,
--     `Sales: Deal Roster` and `Sales: Won Deals With Unconfirmed Orders`. The last also gets its
--     SQLDialectID, which the 6.9 seed's create left unset.
--   * Deal Roster's `PipelineIncludeInForecast` field: Sequence 1 -> 10, its position in the
--     SELECT. The 6.9 seed created it at 1.
--
-- Every updated ID is pinned by an earlier seed (V202608251930, V202609282300), so the updates
-- target the same rows on every host. Nothing new is written to the core schema, so
-- migrations-teardown/ is unchanged.
--
-- NOT INCLUDED -- the ML bench output under metadata/ml-models, ml-training-pipelines,
-- ml-model-scoring-bindings and record-processes. Same decision as the 6.9 and 6.10 seeds;
-- check-release-seed-coverage lists them in HELD_BACK.
--
-- -- TRANSFORMS APPLIED TO THE GENERATOR'S OUTPUT ---------------------------------------------
